Assassin on Xenolink Z3A --- Update 12th June 93
------------------------

A month or so back, I started to convert this rather good game for use on
Xenolink. I got sidetracked doing some other bits and bobs, but I've got round 
finishing it now.

I've ported the TA version, this was not the original version. Roger Clark
did all the hard work with the port to TA.

OK to install is simple. Create a directory in Xdoors: called Assassin. Copy 
all the files from this archive into it. Now move the file Assassin.trans 
( little kickback to TransAmiga :-> ) to your REXX: assign, also move clog.cron 
to your REXX: assign as well. 

Now add the following lines or something similar to one of your menus ( well
I have two DOORS menus ).

CMD = "A"
    {
     REXX "^50000^1^Assassin.trans"
   }

The stack level of 50000 is up to you, I tend to use loads of stack, and I
rarely get problems with any of my doors/utils.

Ok, all should run OK. I've altered some of the text files to be tidier under
Xenolink, and quite heavily edited the main Arexx. As far as I can tell, there
are no bugs in it, if you find any PLEASE let me know, so I can cure them.

Also please read the docs that come with the original file(s), as there is 
a piece on the use of clog.cron.

This will be my last piece of software for Z3A, as Z4 will require some 
changes, and I'm not going to spend time writing stuff that will be useless.


* This version is the one that should have made it out correctly in XENOG *
* It works perfectly on my sys, and I've been playing it now for a month  *
* without any probs. Please check you have installed it correctly if you  *
* do find any problems..............                                      *  

My thanks to the original author, who I've been unable to contact, and to 
Roger Clark for his TA conversion.



Have fun.....

Ciao,

Martin

